+ *     this frame   P  = (u, v, z, 1) . M_cur          (row vector)
+ *     moved        P' = P + (eye_cur - eye_prev)       (same point, seen from the previous eye)
+ *     last frame   (u', v', z', w') = P' . inverse(M_prev)
+ * Objects that move on their own (characters, cars) get the camera's motion
+ * only; the interpolator's own flow estimate has to do the rest.
+ *
+ * Nothing here knows a title: M and the eye are whatever the port hands
+ * over each frame (rsx_draw_engine_framegen_camera), and a port that hands
